{
  "themes": [
    {
      "name": "Detect Pipeline Outage Fallout",
      "definition": "Calls addressing customer impact, root causes, technical remediation, SLA credits, or communication failures related to the March Detect event ingestion pipeline outage.",
      "distinguishing": "Focuses on the acute March platform outage where event ingestion collapsed, unlike general roadmap discussions or individual alert delay troubleshooting.",
      "owner": "support lead",
      "actionable_because": "Support leads can proactively identify affected accounts, deliver technical incident write-ups, and train teams on incident notification protocols.",
      "meeting_ids": ["433FFC", "670E6D", "8C81E8", "A24D4F", "C898C9", "DC6D94", "DC89B6", "EA6697", "EFB1A6"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "433FFC",
          "quote": "So the incident started around 2:14 AM Pacific on March 10th."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "DC89B6",
          "quote": "What I'm seeing is nothing. Literally nothing. Our Detect alerts have not fired once since yesterday evening and we are a retail platform, we have thousands of transactions moving through our infrastructure every hour, and the idea that zero threats have been flagged in that window is — that's not realistic, that's a broken product."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "C898C9",
          "quote": "We had a six-hour window where Aegis Detect just... went dark."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Comply v2 Feature Adoption and Early Access",
      "definition": "Calls where customers inquire about, preview, prepare for, or adopt the new multi-framework on-demand reporting capabilities in Comply v2.",
      "distinguishing": "Focuses specifically on rolling out, adopting, and understanding standard capabilities of the Comply v2 release, rather than custom framework customization or contract renewal negotiations.",
      "owner": "sales / account manager",
      "actionable_because": "Account managers can invite interested customers to product briefings, schedule onboarding demonstrations, and use new compliance capabilities to drive expansions.",
      "meeting_ids": ["174FDD", "8C81E8", "A19AF2", "A24D4F", "EF0B75", "EFB1A6"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "174FDD",
          "quote": "The GA launch is actually scheduled for April 7th, so that's like, what, four days from now."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "A24D4F",
          "quote": "Yeah so, uh, Comply v2 went GA on April 7th — on-demand reporting is live, we've got SOC 2, PCI DSS, HIPAA, and ISO 27001 all supported."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "EF0B75",
          "quote": "So we're launching Comply v2 — it's not out yet but it's coming very soon — and one of the headline features is on-demand compliance reporting."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Custom Compliance Reporting Requests",
      "definition": "Calls where customers explicitly request custom control frameworks, cross-framework control matrices, or bespoke reporting templates beyond standard Comply features.",
      "distinguishing": "Focuses on requests to create bespoke frameworks or cross-framework matrix comparisons not natively supported, rather than learning or adopting standard Comply v2 features.",
      "owner": "product manager",
      "actionable_because": "Product managers can prioritize roadmap requirements and recruit design partners for custom compliance template engines.",
      "meeting_ids": ["00227D", "05678C", "5798C7"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "00227D",
          "quote": "And I'm wondering if there's any way to build a custom template inside Comply that maps to those internal controls."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "05678C",
          "quote": "Like we can pull the report but there's no real way to drill down into specific control areas without basically exporting everything and doing it manually in Excel."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "5798C7",
          "quote": "But what we need is the ability to kind of cross-reference controls across multiple frameworks in a single report."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Contract Renewal and Retention Risk",
      "definition": "Calls focused on commercial contract renewal terms, pricing discussions, SLA concessions, and competitor threats.",
      "distinguishing": "Centers on commercial renewal negotiations and competitor evaluation rather than onboarding setups or standalone incident debugging.",
      "owner": "sales / account manager",
      "actionable_because": "Sales and account managers can structure commercial proposals with SLA commitments and price concessions to prevent churn to competitors.",
      "meeting_ids": ["8C81E8", "C898C9", "EA6697"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "8C81E8",
          "quote": "So Wayne, the whole purpose of today is really just — it's your annual review, renewal's coming up at the end of May, and I want to make sure we're doing right by you before we get into any of that paperwork stuff."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "C898C9",
          "quote": "We've been talking to SentinelShield. They reached out to us actually, right around the time the outage happened — which, great timing on their part."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "EA6697",
          "quote": "We're proposing 99.9% uptime on Detect, which is up from the 99.5% that was in your current contract."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "New Module Onboarding Architecture",
      "definition": "Structured planning or kickoff sessions designed to architect, scope, and implement newly purchased modules like Protect or Identity.",
      "distinguishing": "Focuses on strategic initial deployment planning and workload architecture, as opposed to troubleshooting active break-fix errors or handling renewals.",
      "owner": "sales / account manager",
      "actionable_because": "Account managers and onboarding specialists can produce phased integration checklists and timeline milestones to ensure smooth time-to-value.",
      "meeting_ids": ["71D752", "B0C7D9", "D2AE7F"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "71D752",
          "quote": "Typically for a deployment of your scope — hybrid environment, 40 to 50 workloads — we're looking at a phased approach."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "B0C7D9",
          "quote": "So Raymond, just to set the stage for today — the goal of this workshop is really to dig into your backup strategy, understand your current environment at Vanta Health, and start mapping out how Aegis Protect can fit into what you're already doing, does that sound right to you?"
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "D2AE7F",
          "quote": "So Derek, before I get into the actual deployment steps, can you give me a quick picture of your current identity landscape?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ingestion Pipeline Latency and Connector Failures",
      "definition": "Technical troubleshooting of alert delays, webhook timeouts, or SIEM connector failures caused by ingestion pipeline bottlenecks or circuit breaker settings.",
      "distinguishing": "Deals with ongoing latency, node queue depth imbalance, and SIEM connector timeouts rather than total pipeline downtime outages.",
      "owner": "engineering lead",
      "actionable_because": "Engineering leads can rebalance tenant node distribution, adjust circuit breaker payload thresholds, and enhance connector streaming pipelines.",
      "meeting_ids": ["0D92AB", "670E6D", "DC6D94"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "0D92AB",
          "quote": "Yeah the pipeline latency investigation has been sitting in my queue and honestly the more I dig into it the more I think we have a deeper architectural issue with the event ingestion layer."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "670E6D",
          "quote": "The event timestamp and the alert-sent timestamp in the Aegis payload itself have a 20-plus minute gap."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "DC6D94",
          "quote": "It looks like it's tripping because the payload size on the five-minute batch is exceeding the default threshold that was set in the 4.1.2 build."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Protect Backup Performance and Infrastructure Failures",
      "definition": "Calls addressing degraded backup job throughput, window overages, or complete backup orchestration failures within Aegis Protect.",
      "distinguishing": "Pertains to Protect backup job performance, throughput drops, and orchestration errors, distinct from Detect pipeline failures or Comply reports.",
      "owner": "engineering lead",
      "actionable_because": "Engineering leads can deploy agent compression fixes, rebalance network routing paths, and resolve backup orchestration timeouts.",
      "meeting_ids": ["51360A", "91F2C3", "92B34B"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "51360A",
          "quote": "Zero successful backup jobs since then."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "91F2C3",
          "quote": "Like the benchmarks we ran in January — we're seeing like a 30-something percent reduction in backup window times on the test clusters, which is pretty significant."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "92B34B",
          "quote": "Okay so I'm seeing the backup throughput dropped pretty substantially — it looks like you were averaging around 800 megabytes per second before March 27th and now you're sitting around 180 to 220."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "product_areas": [
    {
      "name": "Aegis Comply",
      "meeting_ids": ["00227D", "01AB1C", "05678C", "174FDD", "5798C7", "8C81E8", "A19AF2", "A24D4F", "C898C9", "D2AE7F", "EA6697", "EF0B75", "EFB1A6"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "00227D",
          "quote": "So I've got the case here, case number 8811, and it looks like you're coming in with a feature request around custom compliance templates in Aegis Comply."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "174FDD",
          "quote": "So, um, we've been on Aegis Comply for about eight months now and it's been really solid for us."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Aegis Detect",
      "meeting_ids": ["01AB1C", "25FEC8", "433FFC", "670E6D", "8C81E8", "A19AF2", "A24D4F", "C898C9", "DC6D94", "DC89B6", "EA6697", "EFB1A6"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "433FFC",
          "quote": "Correct. For approximately six hours, customers were not getting threat monitoring alerts. Events were being generated on their end, but we weren't processing them, so nothing was surfacing in the Detect dashboard."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "670E6D",
          "quote": "We're running LogVault for our primary SIEM integration, and we have Aegis Detect configured to push alerts via webhook."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Aegis Protect",
      "meeting_ids": ["51360A", "71D752", "91F2C3", "92B34B", "B0C7D9"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "51360A",
          "quote": "The case notes mention an API integration error with Aegis Protect but I want to hear it directly from you."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "71D752",
          "quote": "And that's actually one of the areas where Aegis Protect really shines — you get that single pane of glass across your hybrid environment."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Aegis Identity",
      "meeting_ids": ["25FEC8", "B09D1E", "D2AE7F"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "B09D1E",
          "quote": "So it started, um, I'd say around 7 AM this morning, and it's not all users — it seems to be specifically the users who are enrolled in TOTP-based MFA through Aegis Identity, they're getting token validation failures even though the tokens are generating correctly on their authenticator apps."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "D2AE7F",
          "quote": "Phase one is directory sync and SSO configuration — basically getting Aegis Identity talking to your Entra ID environment, setting up the SAML or OIDC connectors, depending on what your apps support."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "other_note": "Calls 01AB1C (billing disputes over Comply/Detect overage fees), 25FEC8 (internal SOC 2 Type II audit readiness review), and B09D1E (tenant-specific TOTP MFA token validation failure) each had unique single-call issues that did not meet the multi-call threshold for a distinct theme."
}
